<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10751" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">contemplātor</span></b> ,
		ōris, m.
		id.. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An observer, surveyor</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">peritissimus,</span>”
				<i>a marksman</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 19, 1, 7</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A contemplator, an observer</i> (very rare): caeli
			ac deorum, * <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc. 1, 28, 69</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mundi animus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Cons. ad Helv. 8, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">astrorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Flor. 4</span></i>
			, n. 18, p. 361, 4.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
